naged WP Host: **SiteGround “GrowBig”** (≈US$20/mo billed annually) – free SSL via Let’s Encrypt, daily backups, SG Security, staging, US-based data centers, GDPR-ready DPA.  \\\\n• Alt Option (commented): AWS Lightsail WordPress (US$5–10/mo) – include extra steps for snapshots & SSL via LetsEncrypt + Cron.  \\\\n• Residents (~100) View protected pages. Board Members (≈5–10) can edit.  \\\\n• Key Plugins: SG Optimizer, SG Security, Simple Membership, User Role Editor, WP Mail SMTP, UpdraftPlus, Contact Form 7, Redirection.\\\\n• Rollback tiers: (a) SiteGround auto daily backup, (b) UpdraftPlus off-site (S3/Google Drive), (c) manual MySQL+wp-content export before major changes.\\\\n\\\\n====================================================================\\\\n1. Provision Hosting & Domain\\\\n1.1 Purchase SiteGround “GrowBig” plan (if new) or create new site in existing account.  \\\\n1.2 Register dunbaroakshoa.com OR update registrar to custom DNS (SiteGround’s NS: `ns1.siteground.net`, `ns2.siteground.net`).  \\\\n1.3 Wait for propagation; verify with `dig dunbaroakshoa.com +short` resolves to SG IP.\\\\n\\\\n2. SSL & Basic Security\\\\n2.1 In SiteGround Site Tools → Security → SSL → “Let’s Encrypt”. Issue certificate for root + `www`.  \\\\n2.2 Enable “HTTPS Enforce” + HSTS in Site Tools.  \\\\n2.3 Turn on SG Security (firewall, login limiter, bot protection).  \\\\n2.4 Create SFTP user with limited perms `<sftp_hoa>` and strong key; disable password auth if desired.\\\\n\\\\n3. WordPress Installation\\\\n3.1 Site Tools → WordPress → Install & Manage → Install new WordPress.\\\\n    • Admin user: `<WP_ADMIN_USER>` (avoid ‘admin’).  \\\\n    • Email: `<admin@dunbaroakshoa.com>` routed via host or Google Workspace.\\\\n3.2 Record generated MySQL credentials securely (SiteGround auto‐creates DB).\\\\n3.3 Force HTTPS: SG Optimizer → Environment → “HTTPS Config” ➜ ON.\\\\n\\\\n4. WordPress Hardening\\\\n4.1 SG Security plugin → Hardenings: Disable XML-RPC, hide WP version, disable file editing.  \\\\n4.2 Edit `wp-config.php`:\\\\n    ```php\\\\n    define('DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true);\\\\n    define('WP_POST_REVISIONS', 5);\\\\n    define('AUTOSAVE_INTERVAL', 120);\\\\n    define('FORCE_SSL_ADMIN', true);\\\\n    define( 'WP_MEMORY_LIMIT', '256M' );\\\\n    ```\\\\n4.3 Change table prefix from default `wp_` during install (`hoa_` example).  \\\\n4.4 Limit login attempts (SG Security covers).  \\\\n4.5 Install Wordfence only if SG Security deemed insufficient (skip to reduce duplication).\\\\n\\\\n5. Theme & Child Theme\\\\n5.1 Install “GeneratePress” (free, lightweight, accessible).  \\\\n5.2 Create child theme:\\\\n    ```bash\\\\n    wp --allow-root scaffold child-theme dunbaroakshoa-child --parent_theme=generatepress --theme_name=\\\\\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA Child\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ```\\\\n5.3 Add custom logo / colors later via Customizer; no branding exists now – use neutral palette (#004d40 teal accents, Sans-Serif fonts).\\\\n\\\\n6. Plugins – Install & Configure\\\\nUsing WP-CLI or WP Admin ➜ Plugins ➜ Add New.\\\\n6.1 **SG Optimizer** (auto-installed).  \\\\n6.2 **Simple Membership** – manage members, restrict pages.  \\\\n6.3 **User Role Editor** – create “Resident” (read), “Board” (edit_others_pages, edit_pages, upload_files).  \\\\n6.4 **WP Mail SMTP** – SMTP host: `<smtp.mailgun.org>` or SiteGround mail; set From address.  \\\\n6.5 **UpdraftPlus** – schedule daily backups to Google Drive bucket `<gdrive-folder-id>`.  \\\\n6.6 **Contact Form 7** – HOA contact form.  \\\\n6.7 **Redirection** – manage 301s if page structure changes.  \\\\n6.8 **Disable Comments** (optional).  \\\\n6.9 Activate & configure each.\\\\n\\\\n7. Membership & Role Setup\\\\n7.1 User Role Editor → Add role “Resident” (clone Subscriber).  \\\\n7.2 Add role “Board” (clone Editor, but remove `edit_theme_options`).\\\\n7.3 Simple Membership → Settings:\\\\n    • Enable WP user integration.  \\\\n    • Membership levels:\\\\n        – Resident (Level ID 2) ➜ 